      "reading": "ちょうこう",
      "reason": "兆候 (choukou) more broadly covers the 'sign', 'symptom', or 'omen' aspects of 'indication', which are often what a general learner would expect for the English word 'indication' in a daily life context. This makes it a more natural and semantically appropriate general replacement than 指示, which is primarily 'instruction'."
